###############################################################
############ API INTEGRATION & STATE MANAGEMENT ################
###############################################################

# OBJECTIVE

Create a clean, scalable and strongly typed frontend integration layer.

The frontend must adapt to the backend.

Never modify backend behavior.

------------------------------------------------------------

# API SOURCE OF TRUTH

API contracts must come ONLY from:

Controllers

Swagger

DTOs

Application Layer

Validators

Never invent request shapes.

Never invent response shapes.

------------------------------------------------------------

# MODEL GENERATION

Generate strongly typed:

Interfaces

DTOs

Models

Enums

Request Objects

Response Objects

Filter Objects

Pagination Objects

Never use:

any

unknown

dynamic structures

------------------------------------------------------------

# MODEL STRUCTURE

Example:

Feature

↓

DTO

↓

Model

↓

Mapper

↓

Component

Never bind backend DTOs directly to UI components.

Always create frontend models if transformation is needed.

------------------------------------------------------------

# API SERVICES

Each feature must contain:

Services

Models

Interfaces

Error handling

Loading state

Mapping

------------------------------------------------------------

# SERVICE RULES

Services should:

Contain API logic only

Contain mapping only

Contain transformations

Never contain UI logic.

Never contain navigation.

Never contain component state.

------------------------------------------------------------

# COMPONENT RULES

Components should never:

Call HttpClient directly

Build URLs

Transform API data

Handle token logic

------------------------------------------------------------

# HTTP STRUCTURE

Backend

↓

Http Client

↓

Interceptor

↓

API Service

↓

State

↓

Component

------------------------------------------------------------

# INTERCEPTORS

Create reusable interceptors:

Authentication Interceptor

Refresh Token Interceptor

Error Interceptor

Loading Interceptor

Request Tracking Interceptor

------------------------------------------------------------

# AUTHENTICATION INTERCEPTOR

Responsibilities:

Attach JWT

Attach headers

Attach authorization

Never duplicate token logic.

------------------------------------------------------------

# REFRESH TOKEN INTERCEPTOR

Responsibilities:

Detect expiration

Refresh automatically

Retry request

Logout if refresh fails

------------------------------------------------------------

# ERROR INTERCEPTOR

Responsibilities:

Handle:

400

401

403

404

409

422

500

Network errors

Unexpected errors

Display appropriate feedback

------------------------------------------------------------

# LOADING INTERCEPTOR

Responsibilities:

Track request count

Show loading state

Hide loading state

Prevent flashing

------------------------------------------------------------

# SIGNALR

Create reusable SignalR service.

Support:

Reconnect

Connection state

Retry

Notifications

Chat

Real-time updates

------------------------------------------------------------

# STATE MANAGEMENT

Preferred order:

Signals

↓

Computed

↓

Effects

↓

RxJS if required

------------------------------------------------------------

# SIGNAL RULES

Use signal():

Local state

UI state

Feature state

Use computed():

Derived state

Statistics

Filters

Use effect():

Reactions

Synchronization

------------------------------------------------------------

# RXJS USAGE

RxJS allowed ONLY for:

HTTP streams

SignalR

Complex async flows

Debounce

Search streams

Never overuse RxJS.

------------------------------------------------------------

# STORE RULES

Store should contain:

State

Actions

Selectors

Loading

Errors

Computed state

------------------------------------------------------------

# SEARCH STATE

Support:

Debounce

Cancel previous request

Pagination reset

Filter reset

------------------------------------------------------------

# PAGINATION STATE

Support:

Current page

Page size

Total count

Loading state

------------------------------------------------------------

# FILTER STATE

Support:

Search

Status

Date range

Dynamic filters

------------------------------------------------------------

# ERROR HANDLING

Every API request must support:

Loading

Error

Retry

Cancellation

Unauthorized

Forbidden

Validation

------------------------------------------------------------

# FILE UPLOAD

Create reusable upload service.

Support:

Single Upload

Multiple Upload

Progress

Cancel

Retry

Validation

Preview

------------------------------------------------------------

# CACHING

Cache only where beneficial.

Examples:

Lookups

Reference data

Settings

Avoid stale business data.

------------------------------------------------------------

# API COMPLETION RULE

Integration is NOT complete unless:

✓ Request typed

✓ Response typed

✓ Error handled

✓ Loading handled

✓ Retry handled

✓ Authentication works

✓ Refresh works

✓ State updated

✓ UI updated

